#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:111
#, xml-text
msgid "Installation of Vim"
msgstr "Instalação do Vim"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:115
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you recompile <application>Vim</application> to link against "
"<application>X</application> and your <application>X</application> libraries"
" are not on the root partition, you will no longer have vim for use in "
"emergencies. You may choose to install an additional editor, not link "
"<application>Vim</application> against <application>X</application>, or move"
" the current <command>vim</command> executable to the <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/bin</filename> directory under a different name such as"
" <filename>vi</filename>."
msgstr ""
"Se recompilar o <application>Vim</application> para se vincular ao "
"<application>X</application> e tuas bibliotecas <application>X</application>"
" não estiverem na partição raiz, você não mais terá vim para uso em "
"emergências. Você pode optar por instalar um editor adicional; não vincular "
"o <application>Vim</application> ao <application>X</application>; ou mover o"
" atual executável <command>vim</command> para o diretório <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/bin</filename> sob um nome diferente, tal como "
"<filename>vi</filename>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:127
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Install <application>Vim</application> by running the following commands:"
msgstr ""
"Instale <application>Vim</application> executando os seguintes comandos:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:133
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If you intend to run the tests and have not installed Xorg in /usr, append "
"LDFLAGS='-L$XORG_PREFIX/lib' to the configure line below."
msgstr ""
"Se você pretende executar os testes e não instalou o Xorg em /usr, [então] "
"anexe LDFLAGS='-L$XORG_PREFIX/lib' à linha de configuração abaixo."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:138
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>echo '#define SYS_VIMRC_FILE  \"/etc/vimrc\"' &gt;&gt;  src/feature.h &amp;&amp;\n"
"echo '#define SYS_GVIMRC_FILE \"/etc/gvimrc\"' &gt;&gt; src/feature.h &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"./configure --prefix=/usr        \\\n"
"            --with-features=huge \\\n"
"            --enable-gui=gtk3    \\\n"
"            --with-tlib=ncursesw &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>echo '#define SYS_VIMRC_FILE  \"/etc/vimrc\"' &gt;&gt;  src/feature.h &amp;&amp;\n"
"echo '#define SYS_GVIMRC_FILE \"/etc/gvimrc\"' &gt;&gt; src/feature.h &amp;&amp;\n"
"\n"
"./configure --prefix=/usr       \\\n"
"            --with-features=huge \\\n"
"            --enable-gui=gtk3    \\\n"
"            --with-tlib=ncursesw &amp;&amp;\n"
"make</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:149
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If the global configuration file <filename>/etc/vimrc</filename> references "
"the <envar>VIMRUNTIME</envar> environment variable, some tests may complain "
"about being unable to find the corresponding directory and wait for user "
"input. If this is the case, this file should be saved and removed before "
"running the tests.  Or if <xref linkend='bubblewrap'/> is installed, it's "
"also possible to create a lightweight container environment where this file "
"is hidden and run the tests in the container."
msgstr ""
"Se o arquivo global de configuração <filename>/etc/vimrc</filename> "
"referenciar a variável de ambiente <envar>VIMRUNTIME</envar>, alguns testes "
"possivelmente reclamem a respeito de estarem inaptos para encontrarem o "
"diretório correspondente e aguardem por entrada gerada do(a) usuário(a). Se "
"esse for o caso, esse arquivo deveria ser salvo e removido antes de executar"
" os testes. Ou se <xref linkend='bubblewrap'/> estiver instalado, também é "
"possível criar um ambiente leve de contêiner onde esse arquivo fique oculto "
"e executar os testes no contêiner."

#.  For vim-9.1.0927 the following flaky tests failed: test_remote.vim,
#.       test_startup.vim, test_termcodes.vim, test_xxd.vim
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:161
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"To test the results, issue: <command>make -j1 test</command>.  Test "
"failures, if any, will produce the file <filename>test.log</filename> in "
"<filename class=\"directory\">src/testdir</filename>. The remaining tests "
"will still be executed. If all goes well, the log will report <literal>ALL "
"DONE</literal>. Some tests labelled as <quote>flaky</quote> may fail "
"occasionally and can be ignored.  The tests are known to fail if the output "
"is redirected to a file, and also if they are run in a 'screen' session."
msgstr ""
"Para testar os resultados, emita: <command>make -j1 test</command>. Falhas "
"de teste, se existirem, produzirão o arquivo <filename>test.log</filename> "
"em <filename class=\"directory\">src/testdir</filename>. Os testes restantes"
" ainda serão executados. Se tudo correr bem, o registro informará "
"<literal>ALL DONE</literal>. Alguns testes rotulados como "
"<quote>escamosos</quote> possivelmente falhem ocasionalmente e podem ser "
"ignorados. Os testes são conhecidos por falharem se a saída gerada for "
"redirecionada para um arquivo e também se forem executados em uma sessão do "
"'screen'."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:176
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"If running the tests with <xref linkend='bubblewrap'/> and "
"<filename>/etc/vimrc</filename> hidden, use <command>bwrap --dev-bind / / "
"--dev-bind /dev/null /etc/vimrc make -j1 test</command>."
msgstr ""
"Se executar os testes com <xref linkend='bubblewrap'/> e "
"<filename>/etc/vimrc</filename> ocultos, use <command>bwrap --dev-bind / / "
"--dev-bind /dev/null /etc/vimrc make -j1 test</command>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><note><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:184
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"Some color tests expect to be executed under the <command>xterm</command> "
"terminal emulator."
msgstr ""
"Alguns testes de cores esperam ser executados sob o emulador de terminal "
"<command>xterm</command>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:190
#, xml-text
msgid "Now, as the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user:"
msgstr ""
"Agora, como o(a) usuário(a) <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem>:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:193
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid "<userinput>make install</userinput>"
msgstr "<userinput>make install</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:196
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"By default, Vim's documentation is installed in <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/share/vim</filename>. The following symlink allows "
"the documentation to be accessed via <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/share/doc/vim-&vim-version;</filename>, making it "
"consistent with the location of documentation for other packages:"
msgstr ""
"Por padrão, a documentação do Vim é instalada em <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/share/vim</filename>. O link simbólico a seguir "
"permite que a documentação seja acessada via <filename "
"class=\"directory\">/usr/share/doc/vim-&vim-version;</filename>, tornando-o "
"consistente com o local da documentação para outros pacotes:"

#.  When updating, be sure to change the vim-majmin entity for the
#.      proper 'vimxx' unpacked directory
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:206
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>ln -snfv ../vim/vim&vim-majmin;/doc /usr/share/doc/vim-&vim-"
"version;</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>ln -snfv ../vim/vim&vim-majmin;/doc /usr/share/doc/vim-&vim-"
"version;</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:209
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<emphasis role='bold'>If</emphasis> you wish to update the runtime files, "
"issue the following command (requires <xref linkend=\"rsync\"/>)  to "
"download it:"
msgstr ""
"<emphasis role='bold'>Se</emphasis> você desejar atualizar os arquivos de "
"tempo de execução, emita o seguinte comando (exige <xref "
"linkend=\"rsync\"/>) para baixá-los:"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:214
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>rsync -avzcP --exclude=\"/dos/\" --exclude=\"/spell/\" \\\n"
"    ftp.nluug.nl::Vim/runtime/ ./runtime/</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>rsync -avzcP --exclude=\"/dos/\" --exclude=\"/spell/\" \\\n"
"    ftp.nluug.nl::Vim/runtime/ ./runtime/</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:218
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"And then install the updated runtime files and regenerate the "
"<filename>tags</filename> file, as the <systemitem "
"class=\"username\">root</systemitem> user issue:"
msgstr ""
"E, então, instalar os arquivos atualizados de tempo de execução e gerar "
"novamente o arquivo <filename>tags</filename>, como o(a) usuário(a) "
"<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>, emita:"

#.  already executed by "make install" if not updating the runtime
#.          files
#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><screen>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:225
#, no-wrap, xml-text
msgid ""
"<userinput>make -C src installruntime &amp;&amp;\n"
"vim -c \":helptags /usr/share/doc/vim-&vim-version;\" -c \":q\"</userinput>"
msgstr ""
"<userinput>make -C src installruntime &amp;&amp;\n"
"vim -c \":helptags /usr/share/doc/vim-&vim-version;\" -c \":q\"</userinput>"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><title>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:231
#, xml-text
msgid "Command Explanations"
msgstr "Explicações do Comando"

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:234
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--with-features=huge</parameter>: This switch enables all the "
"additional features available in <application>Vim</application>, including "
"support for multibyte characters."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--with-features=huge</parameter>: Essa chave habilita todos os "
"recursos adicionais disponíveis no <application>Vim</application>, incluindo"
" suporte para caracteres múltiplos bytes."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:240
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<parameter>--with-tlib=ncursesw</parameter>: This switch forces Vim to link "
"against the <filename class=\"libraryfile\">libncursesw</filename> library."
msgstr ""
"<parameter>--with-tlib=ncursesw</parameter>: Essa chave força o Vim a "
"vincular-se à biblioteca <filename "
"class=\"libraryfile\">libncursesw</filename>."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:246
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--enable-gui=no</option>: This will prevent compilation of the GUI. "
"<application>Vim</application> will still link against "
"<application>X</application>, so that some features such as the client-"
"server model or the x11-selection (clipboard) are still available."
msgstr ""
"<option>--enable-gui=no</option>: Isso impedirá a compilação da GUI. O "
"<application>Vim</application> ainda se vinculará ao "
"<application>X</application>, de modo que alguns recursos, tais como o "
"modelo cliente-servidor ou a seleção x11 (área de transferência), ainda "
"estejam disponíveis."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:253
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--without-x</option>: If you prefer not to link "
"<application>Vim</application> against <application>X</application>, use "
"this switch."
msgstr ""
"<option>--without-x</option>: Se você preferir não vincular o "
"<application>Vim</application> ao <application>X</application>, [então] use "
"essa chave."

#. type: Content of: <sect1><sect2><para>
#: blfs-en/postlfs/editors/vim.xml:259
#, xml-text
msgid ""
"<option>--enable-luainterp</option>, <option>--enable-perlinterp</option>, "
"<option>--enable-python3interp=dynamic</option>, <option>--enable-tclinterp "
"--with-tclsh=tclsh</option>, <option>--enable-rubyinterp</option>: These "
"options include the Lua, Perl, Python3, Tcl, or Ruby interpreters that allow"
" using other application code in <application>vim</application> scripts. All"
" the <option>--enable-*</option> options can accept "
"<option>=dynamic</option> to dynamically load the interpreter when needed. "
"This is required for <application>Python 3</application> to prevent "
"segmentation faults. For <application>tcl</application>, it is necessary to "
"indicate the name of the <command>tclsh</command> executable, since "
"<command>configure</command> only searches versioned names with old "
"versions."
msgstr ""
"<option>--enable-luainterp</option>, <option>--enable-perlinterp</option>, "
"<option>--enable-python3interp=dynamic</option>, <option>--enable-tclinterp "
"--with-tclsh=tclsh</option>, <option>--enable-rubyinterp</option>: Essas "
"opções incluem os interpretadores Lua, Perl, Python3, Tcl ou Ruby que "
"permitem usar código de outro aplicativo em conjuntos de comandos "
"sequenciais do <application>vim</application>. Todas as opções "
"<option>--enable-*</option> conseguem aceitar <option>=dynamic</option> para"
" carregar dinamicamente o interpretador quando necessário. Isso é exigido "
"para <application>Python 3</application> para evitar falhas de segmentação. "
"Para <application>tcl</application>, é necessário indicar o nome do "
"executável <command>tclsh</command>, pois <command>configure</command> "
"somente pesquisa nomes versionados com versões antigas."

